description:
Context

A real claudex-next workflow lost an active Luna response when chatgpt.com closed the upstream WebSocket with close 1006 / unexpected EOF. CLIProxyAPI had already written downstream HTTP 200/SSE headers, then attempted to replace the status with 500 ("Headers were already written"). The Claude workflow marked the agent failed even though earlier edits persisted. Repeated idle i/o timeouts and several close-1006 events were observed in the same run.

Goal

Add narrowly scoped, observable recovery for upstream WebSocket failures without ever duplicating visible output or tool calls. Preserve in-session model switching and session routing.

TDD plan / acceptance criteria

1. RED integration tests using a deterministic fake WebSocket upstream:
- disconnect before any downstream SSE event/bytes: evict the dead connection, redial, replay the buffered request exactly once, and complete one logical downstream response;
- disconnect after any downstream event/bytes (including reasoning): do not replay; emit exactly one valid terminal SSE error and do not attempt to rewrite HTTP status after headers are committed;
- second disconnect after the single retry: terminate cleanly with one downstream error;
- client cancellation, auth/protocol errors, and explicitly non-retriable closes never retry;
- retry cannot duplicate response items or tool calls.

2. RED regression coverage for in-session model switching:
- successive requests in one Claude session may select different configured models;
- a pre-output retry preserves the model selected for that request, credentials, effort, and conversation/session metadata;
- retry does not pin later requests to the prior model or stale upstream connection.

3. RED pool/liveness tests:
- timed-out/closed pooled sockets are evicted and never reused;
- concurrent requests cannot race reuse of a failed connection;
- request body/replay state is bounded and released on completion/cancellation.

4. GREEN implementation:
- allow at most one transparent retry, only while zero downstream events/bytes have been emitted;
- track committed-stream state explicitly rather than inferring it from an HTTP write failure;
- after commitment, preserve HTTP 200 and encode the failure solely as a valid SSE error/terminal event;
- keep retry policy in the proxy transport layer, with no orchestration-level replay after partial output.

5. Observability:
- metrics count disconnects, retries attempted/succeeded/exhausted/suppressed, classified by bounded reason and pre/post-output boundary;
- spans/events record attempt number, connection eviction/redial, retry decision, first-downstream-event boundary, and terminal outcome;
- logs correlate request/session safely and state why retry was allowed or suppressed;
- no prompts, response payloads, credentials, or unbounded error strings in telemetry.

6. Verification:
- focused unit/integration tests pass under -race;
- existing Claude WebSocket, SSE translation, classifier rerouting, alias routing, and in-session model-switching suites remain green;
- add a local e2e fault-injection scenario and document how to inspect its Prometheus metrics and Tempo trace.

Non-goals

Do not transparently replay after reasoning, visible text, response items, or tool calls have reached Claude. Do not attempt to fix Claude Code workflow reconciliation in this proxy task.
